# Environment Variables

## Required Variables

```bash
# Master encryption key for the entire system
# Must be 32+ bytes, randomly generated
# Generate with: openssl rand -hex 32
ARCA_MASTER_KEY=your-master-key-here-min-32-chars

# Encryption key for client data
# Must be 32+ bytes, randomly generated
# Generate with: openssl rand -hex 32
ARCA_ENCRYPTION_KEY=your-encryption-key-here-min-32-chars

# Internal API key for system access
# Must be randomly generated
# Generate with: openssl rand -hex 32
INTERNAL_AFIP_API_KEY=your-internal-key-here

# Google Cloud service account JSON
# Download from GCP > IAM > Service Accounts > Keys
GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS={"type":"service_account",...}
```

## Optional Variables

```bash
# AFIP default access token (fallback if client doesn't provide)
# Only for development/testing
AFIP_ACCESS_TOKEN=your-afip-token

# Node environment
NODE_ENV=production

# Log level
LOG_LEVEL=info
```

## How to Generate Keys

```bash
# Generate master key
openssl rand -hex 32

# Generate encryption key
openssl rand -hex 32

# Generate internal API key
openssl rand -hex 32

# Generate AFIP access token (from AFIP portal)
# Only for development use
```

## Security Notes

- NEVER commit these variables to version control
- Store them securely (GCP Secret Manager recommended)
- Rotate keys periodically
- Each key should be unique and randomly generated
- Master key should be backed up securely offline